  "answer_text": "It looks like you're referring to a **GMAT Sentence Correction** question! Here is a full breakdown of the question and its answer:\n\n---\n\n### The Question\n\n**\"Unable to build nests or care for their young, a female cowbird lays up to 40 eggs a year in the nests of other birds, including warblers, vireos, flycatchers, and thrushes.\"**\n\nThe answer choices are:\n\n\n- **A.** a female cowbird lays up to 40 eggs a year in the nests of other birds, including\n- **B.** a female cowbird will use the nests of other birds to lay up to 40 eggs a year, including those of\n- **C.** female cowbirds use the nests of other birds to lay up to 40 eggs a year, including those of\n- **D.** female cowbirds lay up to 40 eggs a year in the nests of other birds, including\n- **E.** up to 40 eggs a year are laid by female cowbirds in the nests of other birds, including\n\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Correct Answer: **D**\n\n---\n\n### Explanation\n\n**Why A and B are wrong:**\nIn A and B, *their* (plural) does not agree with *a female cowbird* (singular).\n\n**Why C is wrong:**\nIn C, *\"female cowbirds...lay up to 40 eggs a year, including those of warblers\"* \u2014 here, *those* seems to refer to eggs (the nearest preceding plural noun), yielding the meaning that female cowbirds lay the eggs **of** warblers, which is not the intended meaning.\n\n**Why E is wrong:**\nE is out due to incorrect modification.\n\n**Why D is correct:**\nThe first major problem is the modifier *\"Unable to build nests or care for their young.\"* This modifier must be followed by *'female cowbirds'*. Notice that the modifier says *\"care for their young,\"* so it needs the **plural** form of cowbird. Only **D** correctly places *\"female cowbirds\"* immediately after the opening modifier and avoids the ambiguity of *\"those of\"* found in C.\n\n---\n\n### Key Grammar Concept: **Dangling/Misplaced Modifiers**\nThe opening participial phrase *\"Unable to build nests or care for their young\"* must directly and logically modify the **subject** of the main clause. The subject must be the one who is unable to build nests \u2014 that is, **female cowbirds** (plural). Only **D** satisfies both the modifier placement and the pronoun agreement requirements.",
